-- title:
--   Commutative lift of widehatE₀ over W₀[[t]] with normalised q-series
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \neq 2$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, and let $E_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ which is elliptic (unit discriminant) and whose formal group $\widehat{E_0}$, built from the fixed Weierstrass formal group law `formalGroupLawFixed`, satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`: taking the ideal $\bot$ as the adic structure, there is a unit $u \in k[[Z]]$ with $[q]_{\widehat{E_0}} = u \cdot \widehat{E_0}.\mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\,q\,0\,0$, where $[n]$ denotes the series `nthSeries` defined by $[0] = 0$ and $[n+1] = F([n](Z), Z)$. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, and let $\mathrm{res}_0 \colon W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal. Then there exists a formal group law $F^u$ over $W_0[[t]]$ which is commutative, which lifts $\widehat{E_0}$ in the sense that the two-variable power series of $\widehat{E_0}$ is the image of that of $F^u$ under the map induced by $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, and for which the coefficient of $t$ in the coefficient of $Z^q$ in $[q]_{F^u}$ is congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   This is the deformation-theoretic input producing a one-parameter lift of a height-two formal group over $W_0[[t]]$ whose $q$-series has first-order coefficient a unit normalised to $1$ — the formal-group shadow of the fact that the Hasse invariant of the universal deformation has a simple zero. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of completions of modular curves of full level and of the associated level moduli packages.
-- source:
